message: "If you use, adapt, or teach with this model, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Compatible-Section Bed Sharing and Behavioural Risk in a Shared Medical-Tourism Hospital Department: A Hybrid Agent-Based and Discrete-Event Simulation"
abstract: >-
  A behaviour-explicit hybrid agent-based and discrete-event simulation, built in AnyLogic,
  of a multi-specialty international-patient hospital department serving medical tourists and
  local patients from the same beds, specialists and appointment slots. Patient behaviour
  (medication adherence, doctor switching, channel choice and early abandonment) is part of
  the operational logic rather than post-hoc discussion, and compatible wards borrow each
  other's idle beds through inter-agent message passing. Across 30 randomized-seed
  replications, compatible-section bed sharing reduces the mean inpatient admission queue by
  43 percent against an otherwise identical discrete-event-only model.
